fcitx5-ngosen (1:1.5.5-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Recognise Flatpak apps by their usual program name, so Firefox from Flatpak no longer mixes
    up words while autofilling an address (#200, #204).
  * Macros with an uppercase abbreviation such as VN now expand (#194).
  * Sen mode: backspacing into the last word no longer rebuilds macro text that ends in a quote
    or ellipsis, or a word in a legacy charset; found by a test (#199).
  * Typing the next letter of an address Firefox is autofilling is no longer taken for a click,
    so gox gives gõ and daaus gives dấu (#209).

 -- Nguyen Phi <nguyenphidt@gmail.com>  Tue, 20 Oct 2026 23:00:00 +0700

